      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5f3d715449557333b392b50e|full_name}: See, the problem with people hiding avatars or just not happening to see symbols on avatars is why it would be better if it was a thing to attach to your nameplate. Expecting everyone to add things their avatars, when most people don't even know how to upload one in the first place, is also the opposite of user friendly design. People are significantly less likely to be hiding name plates, so the nameplate would almost immediately be seen. Everyone would also be able to see what any of the symbols mean just by looking at the menu where they can select nameplate badges. Basically I don't see a serious negative of having this as an available feature. Making people change their name to try to add identity markers in would also not work as well because you can't put the needed symbols in the available text format and it would probably consume too much text space.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-08-18T00:44:50.320Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "This is something that one of my closest friends, who is trans MtF pan, really wishes this game had. She suffers chronic anxiety and hates that her voice isn't considered \"gender conformative\" while in real life she completely passes as female and is almost never questioned even if she talks. People in VRC can't see the way you look and present yourself and automatically assume you're male/female based on your voice. She often has people literally reject her professed gender identity when she tries to tell them, which due to her anxiety often leads her to avoid trying to tell people or correct them.\nI feel that a chosen sex/gender symbol on the nameplate can help, especially in cases of people who have anxiety and have trouble confronting people to defend themselves.\n\nIt should include as wide a range of sex/gender identity symbols as possible, ex. trans MTF/FTM, gay, bi, cis male/female, fluid, nonbinary, etc. You can choose as many or as few as you want, or none at all.\n\n(obviously here should be a limitation on taking directly contradictory symbols)\n\nPlayer reporting should also include the option to report people for deliberately misgendering in direct conflict with a person's displayed profile symbol. If it's something shown right there in an official capacity, you are expected to respect it.",
